# Tidy

**Teach a ~{{const.budget_usd}} robot arm household chores from about {{const.n_videos}} phone videos of you doing the chore. No teleoperation. The robot asks for the one extra demo it is least sure about, and retries the step it got wrong.**

> **Evidence stage: everything below is `sim`.** The results come from a MuJoCo digital twin of an SO-100-class arm with *synthetic* phone videos, a simulated hand-pose estimator and a simulated teleoperator. No real-robot result exists yet: no arm has been bought or assembled (`BLOCKERS.md`). Every real-robot step is scripted in `HUMAN_TODO.md` and `SESSION_QUEUE.md`. Every number here is generated from `results/` (`make paper`) and checked by `bench/check_claims.py`.

## System

```
 phone video ─► hands · objects · mat markers · depth ─► grasp/release events ─► task program ("pen → tray, cup stays")
                                                                │
                 retarget: thumb–index → parallel jaw, vertical final approach, IK filter, object-centric targets
                                                                │
                      pseudo-demos ─► ACT ensemble ─► uncertainty ─► "Place the box at B2 … show me the pick"
                                                                │
 overhead cam ─► executor: ready pose → policy → failure detector → retreat + retry / ask for help
                                                                │
                 IK ─► SafeController (joint/velocity/effort limits, workspace box, e-stop, watchdog, proximity) ─► arm
```

