## Quick start

```bash
make setup               # uv venv + pinned deps (requirements.lock)
make test                # unit + safety tests (CI also runs lint, mypy, sim smoke, repo scan)
make reproduce-quick     # every experiment at smoke scale, < 1 h on a laptop CPU
make teach-demo          # the teaching app, end to end, in the twin
make reproduce-full      # the full experiment set (hours on 16 cores)
make paper               # figures + results/INDEX.md + README/paper/bullets from results/, then the claim check
```

Teaching app: `python scripts/teach.py --help` (new chore → filming guide → upload → process → train → try → requests → record).

## Real robot: safety notes

* The real arm can **only** be moved by `scripts/supervised_session.py`. It refuses to start without an interactive operator typing the presence phrase, re-confirms presence every five minutes and before every trial, and refuses while `SAFETY_LOG.md` has unresolved entries. The agent that built this repo never runs it.
* Limits are enforced in code below the policy (`safety/`): joint position/velocity/effort, a Cartesian box, no-go zones, a latching e-stop polled every tick, a watchdog freeze, and a camera person-proximity pause. CI tests fail if any limit can be exceeded or the e-stop check is removed.
* Keep children and pets away. No knives, hot items, liquids or glass. Never leave the arm powered and unattended.
* Privacy: raw phone videos stay in git-ignored `data/private/`. Only processed trajectories are released, and any published frame is face-blurred.

